ATLAS FINAL COMBINED UPDATE
Command Center menu + three glitch fixes

IMPORTANT
Do both parts below. The GitHub upload updates the app, while the Supabase SQL
fixes the warehouse data and installs the corrected location-saving function.

PART 1 — RUN THE SUPABASE FIX

1. Sign in to Supabase and open the ATLAS project.
2. Open SQL Editor.
3. Choose New query.
4. Open ATLAS-SUPABASE-GLITCH-FIX.sql from this package.
5. Copy the entire file into the SQL Editor.
6. Click Run.
7. The final verification result should show zero rows.

If an earlier copy showed a locations_section_valid error, simply run the
updated SQL file from the beginning. The failed transaction did not partially
apply the previous changes.

This step:
- Converts Aisle 22 LEFT/MIDDLE/RIGHT records to Section A/B/C.
- Replaces the old Aisle 22 section constraint with the A/B/C warehouse rule.
- Installs correct_inventory_location without the ambiguous pick_first error.
- Preserves Pick First when a bad duplicate location is removed.

PART 2 — UPLOAD THE WEBSITE TO GITHUB

1. Unzip ATLAS-FINAL-COMBINED-UPDATE.zip on your laptop.
2. Open https://github.com/zmoffett1993/ATLAS
3. Make sure the branch selector says main.
4. Click Add file, then Upload files.
5. Open the unzipped folder and drag these THREE files onto the GitHub upload
   page:
   - index.html
   - service-worker.js
   - atlas-command-center-menu.jpeg
   Do not upload the ZIP itself.
6. GitHub will show index.html and service-worker.js being replaced and the
   approved menu artwork being added.
7. Use this commit message:
   Install Command Center menu and ATLAS glitch fixes
8. Commit directly to the main branch.
9. Wait about two minutes for GitHub Pages to redeploy.

PART 3 — LOAD THE NEW VERSION

1. Close every open ATLAS tab or installed ATLAS app window.
2. Reopen ATLAS and refresh once.
3. If the old menu still appears, delete the installed ATLAS shortcut/app and
   add it to the Home Screen again. The service-worker version was changed so
   the new files replace the old cached version.

VERIFY

- Menu: dark Command Center header and four full-width horizontal menu rows.
- Aisle 22: Section A · Left, Section B · Middle, Section C · Right.
- Product Is Missing: saving a correction succeeds without the pick_first error.
- Camera search: test both a stacked pallet label and a one-line box label.

FILES CHANGED

- index.html
- service-worker.js
- atlas-command-center-menu.jpeg
- ATLAS-SUPABASE-GLITCH-FIX.sql
